abstract: >-
  Exact finite-horizon failure envelopes and reproducible scheduling experiments
  for two binary Markov erasure paths with specified conditional marginal laws
  and unknown causal dependence. Includes exhaustive optimization, a packet-exchange
  heuristic, independent optimization checks, and Monte Carlo validation.
keywords:
  - multipath communication
  - deadline reliability
  - erasure coding
  - robust scheduling
  - causal coupling
